Linux check in Docker (native arm64 on Apple silicon). Needs a running Docker.
Run: scripts/linux-check/run.sh [SOURCE_DIR] [build test clippy node snap bus]   (default: this checkout, all steps).
`bus` runs the D-Bus tests (the tray's StatusNotifierItem and menu, read by a fake tray host) on a private session bus.
It mounts the source read-only and copies it in; cargo's cache and target live in docker volumes uzu-linux-cargo and uzu-linux-target.
Logs and snaps go to /tmp/linux-check/<folder name>/. Compare clippy by running it on main's checkout too.
LINUX_CHECK_VOLUMES=<prefix> uses <prefix>-cargo and <prefix>-target instead (a parallel session).
Remove the volumes with: docker volume rm uzu-linux-cargo uzu-linux-target
Headless snaps need a software GL renderer that supports f16 shaders: Debian trixie's Mesa does (WGPU_BACKEND=gl, the default here); bookworm's lavapipe/llvmpipe does not.
